; --script reads each command line whole, however long.  The script's
; first line is a 1502-character comment and its second a 2035-character
; `bal` command, both past the old 1023-byte line buffer; its last line
; has no trailing newline.  Each command must run, in order.

2012-03-17 KFC
    Expenses:Food                20 CAD
    Assets:Cash

test --script test/regress/script-long-line.dat
              20 CAD  Expenses:Food
12-Mar-17 KFC                   Assets:Cash                 -20 CAD      -20 CAD
end test
